<title>INDIA: India's Century Tex 1996/97 net falls.</title>
<headline>India's Century Tex 1996/97 net falls.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		  26.7  vs    1,947.5</p>
<p>    Gross profit	   1,293.7  vs    2,867.3</p>
<p>    Gross sales	   19,907.6  vs   17,788.8</p>
<p>    Div (in percent)	  60.0  vs	 60.0</p>
<p>    Depreciation	   1,237.4  vs	909.0</p>
<p>    Tax			    1.5  vs	  1.5</p>
<p>    Prior year		  28.1  vs	  9.3</p>
<p>adjustments  </p>
<p>Note: Century Textiles &amp; Industries Limited said adverse market conditions in cement and paper and teething troubles at its Bagasse-based paper plant, a steep decline in dry bulk freight rate in shipping and high interest rate contributed to the lower net profit.</p>
<p>The higher interest burden was due to the fact that the Bagasse-based paper project, the new cement project at Maihar and some other capital expenses have been financed from loans.</p>
<p>Severe power cuts in the central state of Madhya Pradesh, ranging from 40-60 percent over a long period and frequent unscheduled cuts also led to the company's lower profits.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 90000</p>
</text>
